# Reviewed digest manifest for the migration set (REV-039-F01, REV-041-F01).
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT.
#
# Proves: an applied migration file has not changed since it was applied,
#         because `db migrate` records the digest it actually executed and
#         marks it `digest_origin = applied`.
#
# Does NOT prove: which bytes ran on a database migrated BEFORE digests
#         existed. A filename-only ledger row records a NAME, not contents.
#         `1013_strategy_lab.sql` is a real counter-example in this repo
#         (two revisions, two different constraint names).
#
#         Such rows are stored as `baseline:<digest>` with
#         `digest_origin = baseline`, only via
#         `db migrate --accept-legacy-baseline`. `db status` lists them.
#
# Regenerate deliberately, never as part of a deploy.
# Format: <sha256>  <filename>   (digest over LF-normalized bytes)

